"75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-105102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $v=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find $4v+2w.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-105102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply each component of $v$ by $4$ and each component of $w$ by $2.$ Then, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4v+2w & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 18 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}20+(-2) \\\\ -12+18 \\\\ 8+(-4) \\\\ -4+6 \\\\ 0+(-2)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}18 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-105102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d61b54b933e218322ca738b2b317f663e9af4d08773e3b029d666bf4b3c0dcf"} {"question" "q-105102" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capt