17b4276"} {"question" "q-34166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}+{p}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}+{p}_{3}\\cdot {q}_{3}+{p}_{4}\\cdot {q}_{4}+{p}_{5}\\cdot {q}_{5} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-3)+(-2)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-10-4-4-9-10 \\\\  & =-37\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-34166" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d61b54b933e218322ca738b2b317f663e9af4d08773e3b029d666bf4b3c0dcf"} {"question" "q-34166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-34166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-20"] ["math" "-28"] ["math" "-37"] ["math" "8"] ["math" "9"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-34166" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-37"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-73948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $v=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 2x \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}3x \\\\ -3 \\\\ x \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\nIf $v\\cdot w=-2$ and $x>0$, find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-73948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Starting from the equation $v\\cdot w=-2,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot w & =-2 \\\\ x\\cdot 3x+2x\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot x+(-5)\\cdot 2 & =-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-6x+4x-10 & =-2 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-2x-8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the quadratic formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(3)(-8)}}{2(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{100}}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 10}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\pm 5}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get two solutions, ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{4}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=2.$ Since we need $x>0$, our final answer is $x=2$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-73948" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d61b54b933e218322ca738b2b317f663e9af4d08773e3b029d666bf4b3c0dcf"} {"question" "q-73948" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_wi