"answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-34169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $u=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{4} \\\\ 4 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $v=[\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{-2} \\\\ -8x \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ If $u\\cdot v=12$ and $x<6$, find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-34169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Starting from the equation $u\\cdot v=12,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & =12 \\\\ 2{x}^{4}\\cdot 2{x}^{-2}+4\\cdot (-8x)+12\\cdot 4+6\\cdot 2 & =12 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-32x+48+12 & =12 \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-32x+48 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-8x+12 & =0 \\\\ (x-2)(x-6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe get two solutions, ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=6.$ Since we need $x<6$, our final answer is $x=2$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-34169" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d61b54b933e218322ca738b2b317f663e9af4d08773e3b029d666bf4b3c0dcf"} {"question" "q-34169" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-34169" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-34169" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-105110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let\n$p=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ y-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $q=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].$\nIf $p\\cdot q=0$, find the value of $y.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-105110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Starting from the equation $p\\cdot q=0,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $y$ and then solve for $y$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 9\\cdot 0+(y-3)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot y & =0 \\\\ y-3-12+4y & =0 \\\\ 5y & =15 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-105110" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d61b54b933e218322ca738b2b317f663e9af4d08773e3b029d666bf4b3c0dcf"} {"question" "q-105110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-105110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "q-105110" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/state.json" "file_sha256" "75661d8cdcfeae369dbfac0e887fbab0e2fb2a4c43ef6ceec0b8a442517b4276"} {"question" "e-4782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ Find $\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathbf{a}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/example-4782.json" "file_sha256" "5aa61c3f8067abdad022bf03e462a8fe59f3132886923886ec6163e9b6c53bd5"} {"question" "e-4782" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Multiplying each component of $\\mathbf{a}$ by $\\dfrac{1}{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}a & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-4) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/example-4782.json" "file_sha256" "5aa61c3f8067abdad022bf03e462a8fe59f3132886923886ec6163e9b6c53bd5"} {"question" "e-4783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}]$ Find $\\dfrac{1}{3}\\mathbf{a}+\\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/example-4783.json" "file_sha256" "74ce80e8783eb6c993c403203a8836336ee4d803778026dfc4efc4d5f8a75b57"} {"question" "e-4783" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we multiply each component of $\\mathbf{a}$ by $\\dfrac{1}{3}$ and each component of $\\mathbf{b}$ by $\\dfrac{1}{2}.$ Then, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}a+\\frac{1}{2}b & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1-2 \\\\ 2-3 \\\\ 4+1 \\\\ -3-4 \\\\ 1+5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/example-4783.json" "file_sha256" "74ce80e8783eb6c993c403203a8836336ee4d803778026dfc4efc4d5f8a75b57"} {"question" "e-4784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ then what is $\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/example-4784.json" "file_sha256" "41ba85581700a53852ce54e229449d8f88529bca2760e87de92427481754198a"} {"question" "e-4784" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\cdot v & ={u}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}+{u}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}+{u}_{3}\\cdot {v}_{3}+{u}_{4}\\cdot {v}_{4} \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 3+3\\cdot (-4)+(-5)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =2+12-12-30 \\\\  & =-28\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/example-4784.json" "file_sha256" "41ba85581700a53852ce54e229449d8f88529bca2760e87de92427481754198a"} {"question" "e-4785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let be $[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ x \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ x \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]$ If $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=0,$ find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/example-4785.json" "file_sha256" "499a72033a364fdbdaefe8ea283c10083dd574244ed4461fa37f88f7f3af2459"} {"question" "e-4785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Starting from the equation $\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}=0,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 10\\cdot x+x\\cdot x+0\\cdot 8+5\\cdot 5 & =0 \\\\ 10x+{x}^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+10x+25 & =0 \\\\ (x+5)^{2} & =0 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $x=-5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14037236/example-4785.json" "file_sha256" "499a72033a364fdbdaefe8ea283c10083dd574244ed4461fa37f88f7f3af2459"}] "usage" {"q-34227" [] "e-4785" [] "e-4784" [] "e-4782" [] "q-35097" [] "q-34223" [] "e-4783" []} "basis" 1276 "retractions" [[17592186120301 :question/problem "Let $u = \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $-\\frac{1}{3}u$."] [17592186120240 :question/problem "Let $a = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$. Find $3a + 2b$."] [17592186120241 :question/problem "If $u = \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $v = \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}$, then $u \\cdot v =$"] [17592186119539 :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ Find $\\dfrac{1}{2} \\mathbf{a}$."] [17592186119539 :question/worked-solution "Multiplying each component of $\\mathbf{a}$ by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{2}a &= \\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot (-4) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 6 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119540 :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}$ Find $\\dfrac{1}{3}\\mathbf{a}+\\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{b}$."] [17592186119540 :question/worked-solution "First, we multiply each component of $\\mathbf{a}$ by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nand each component of $\\mathbf{b}$ by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nThen, we add the vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{1}{3}a + \\frac{1}{2}b &= \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 12 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} + \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-1 - 2 \\\\ 2 - 3 \\\\ 4 + 1 \\\\ -3 - 4 \\\\ 1 + 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119541 :question/problem "If $\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}$ then what is $\\mathbf{u} \\cdot \\mathbf{v}$?"] [17592186119541 :question/worked-solution "To compute the dot product, we add up the products of corresponding components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu \\cdot v &= u_{1} \\cdot v_{1} + u_{2} \\cdot v_{2} + u_{3} \\cdot v_{3} + u_{4} \\cdot v_{4} \\\\\n&= (-1) \\cdot (-2) + 4 \\cdot 3 + 3 \\cdot (-4) + (-5) \\cdot 6 \\\\\n&= 2 + 12 - 12 - 30 \\\\\n&=-28\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186119542 :question/problem "Let be $\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ x \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ x \\\\ 8 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}$ If $\\mathbf{a}\\cdot \\mathbf{b}=0$, find the value of $x$."] [17592186119542 :question/worked-solution "Starting from the equation\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a} \\cdot \\mathbf{b}=0\n$$\n\nwe compute the dot product in terms of $x$ and then solve for $x$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na \\cdot b &= 0 \\\\\n10 \\cdot x + x \\cdot x + 0 \\cdot 8 + 5 \\cdot 5 &= 0 \\\\\n10x + x^{2} + 25 &= 0 \\\\\nx^{2} + 10x + 25 &= 0 \\\\\n(x + 5)^{2} &= 0 \\\\\nx &= -5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $x=-5$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186117941 17592186117942 17592186117943 17592186117944 17592186117945 17592186117947 17592186117948 17592186117949 17592186117950 17592186117951 17592186118282 17592186118283 17592186118284 17592186118285 17592186118286] "immutable_fields" [[17592186117940 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117940 :answer-field/id] [17592186117940 :answer-field/key] [17592186117940 :answer-field/type] [17592186117946 :answer-field/correct] [17592186117946 :answer-field/id] [17592186117946 :answer-field/key] [17592186117946 :answer-field/type] [17592186118281 :answer-field/correct] [17592186118281 :answer-field/id] [17592186118281 :answer-field/key] [17592186118281 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
